+A 19-language language pack for DSH i18n (ja/ko/fr/...), written for the native
+language-pack API of dsh v0.1.2-alpha.2: each curated language is added to
+DSH's own locale catalog through `ctx.locale.addLanguage`, so it appears in the
+Settings → General Language row alongside 中文/English; its partial
+dictionaries are contributed per namespace through
+`ctx.locale.register(ns, locale, dict)`; the selection persists as DSH's
+durable `locale.preference` setting; and uncovered keys fall back along the
+declared chain (ja/ko/fr → en, then `common`). Client-only plugin — the host
+half is a no-op stub whose row exists because the client module registry
+composes browser rows only for live Loader entries declaring `dsh.client`.
+
+Migrated from the 0.1.1-era form (see `6770ca4`), where DSH had no language
+API: those entry points and their replacements are
+
+| 0.1.1-era entry point | Now owned by DSH |
+|---|---|
+| `LocaleRuntime.prototype.lookup` monkey-patch (third language won only while the active locale stayed `en`) | `ctx.locale.addLanguage` + the native per-key fallback chain; the selected language is the active locale |
+| custom `better-locale` row in `settings.general.item` | DSH's own Language row in the same slot, which lists every registered language |
+| `dsh-plugin-better-locale:active` in localStorage | durable `locale.preference` in `$DSH_HOME/settings.yaml` |
+| `betterLocale` service for third-party dictionaries | `ctx.locale.register(ns, locale, dict)` directly |
+
+`client.js` ships as the lazy-CJS client bundle the release serves from the
+package's `./client` export (`window.__ModuleLoader__.load({ id, factory })`).
 
 Release procedure (internal):
 
